    <edge source="Scrooge" target="Marley's Ghost">
      <data key="d7">6.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Ebenezer Scrooge encounters the ghost of Jacob Marley in the pivotal scene known as Marley's Ghost.&lt;SEP&gt;When Scrooge asks Marley's ghost who it was in life, the ghost responds that he was Scrooge's business partner, Jacob Marley.&lt;SEP&gt;Despite seeing and feeling the presence of Marley's ghost, Scrooge is still incredulous about its reality.&lt;SEP&gt;Scrooge shows fear and respect towards Marley's Ghost, acknowledging its supernatural power.&lt;SEP&gt;Marley's Ghost appears to Scrooge as a supernatural warning about his own fate.&lt;SEP&gt;The warning from Marley's Ghost sets the stage for The Ghost of Christmas Past's appearance to Scrooge.</data>
      <data key="d9">character interaction,fear,fictional event,incredulity,questioning,reaction,respect,skepticism,supernatural connection,warning</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-ea0dd54b1efa58e8a89cfc1597a7aef2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8744a39345dd8d5c2e23dc4c5974d90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf42c25cc5f1283160fc9b776e791663&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-674266fcc96dc2c80a6642653574a251&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a76055a2c7afe2fed010f2b31fbb8c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb3d54efe1e83cfa271d9e8c890a144</data>
